# ── Written into the repository because the service user lives in it ──────
#
# Each tenant's system user has its home set to the application directory, so
# anything a tool writes to $HOME lands beside the source: npm's cache, and the
# .cache / .config that npm, prisma and Next create on a whim.
#
# They are not edits and they are not artifacts worth keeping — but they made
# the deploy guard refuse to run, mid-release, on a live restaurant with the
# migrations already applied. That is the whole cost of leaving junk untracked:
# not the junk, the check that trips over it at the worst moment.
.npm/
/.cache/
/.config/
/.local/

# Scratch and rollback copies of the build. `scripts/deploy.sh` builds into
# .next-build, keeps the outgoing build in .next-previous, and parks a build
# that failed to start in .next-failed.
/.next-build
/.next-previous
/.next-failed
